// What roadmap §B1 actually does, which is not what §B1 says it does.
//
// The row reads *"`file_read` of a missing file answers `""` — indistinguishable from an empty
// file"*, and `lib/files.bx`'s own comment said the same thing for as long as the row existed.
// **Neither is true.** `read_file` on a path it cannot open does not answer; it ends the process
// with exit 70, and this fixture is the measurement that says so.
//
// That makes the bug worse rather than smaller: a silent wrong answer can be checked for
// afterwards, and a program that has stopped cannot check for anything. There was simply **no way
// to read a file that might not be there** — `src/burxt-compiler/lsp.bx` had already worked that
// out for itself and refuses to use the module loader because of it.
//
// `file_read_maybe` is the fix and `tests/pass/files_library.bx` is where it is exercised. This
// fixture stays because a `pass` test cannot pin behaviour that terminates the program, and
// because the next person to read §B1 should find the correction next to the claim.
use "../../lib/files.bx";

region main {
    // Nothing creates this path, and the name is long enough that nothing else will.
    let text: String = file_read("burxt-no-such-file-4c1b9e7a2d");
    print(len(text));
}
